From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 01:26:26 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 252/342] meson_decoder: MPEG-1 and MPEG-2 video on the S905's
 decoder

The plugin takes what FFmpeg's reader calls MPEG-1 or MPEG-2 video too,
4:2:0 up to 1920x1088, with linux-firmware's gxl_mpeg12.bin (in
meson_vdec_firmware). The sequence header comes from the container's
codec data (Matroska, MP4), or for MPEG program and transport streams,
which have none, from the stream: the first one is kept and goes before
every session's stream, after a seek too. 4:2:2 and larger pictures go
to FFmpeg. Interlaced pictures come back as woven frames, as FFmpeg's.

After the last chunk the plugin waits 100 ms for the firmware to finish
before asking for the end of the stream (MPEG-1/2's end code goes in
once the firmware is idle; meanwhile frames must be taken).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
